WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.441
Five servers keep the same log of payments.

2
00:00:05.441 --> 00:00:09.775
Raft picks one leader to take every write and copy it to the others.

3
00:00:09.967 --> 00:00:12.266
All start as followers in term 0.

4
00:00:12.266 --> 00:00:15.889
A term is a numbered period with at most one leader.

5
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:24.085
A follower that hears from no leader starts an election, after a random wait of 150 to 300 milliseconds.

6
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:28.275
S3 drew the shortest, 162 milliseconds.

7
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:35.035
It moves to term 1, becomes a candidate, votes for itself, and asks the others with RequestVote.

8
00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:39.877
Each server grants one vote per term, written to disk first.

9
00:00:39.877 --> 00:00:41.592
S1, S2 and S4 say yes.

10
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.315
With 4 votes of 5, a majority, S3 leads term 1.

11
00:00:45.315 --> 00:00:50.888
Its heartbeat, every 50 milliseconds, keeps the others from starting elections.

12
00:00:51.067 --> 00:00:52.499
A client sends pay-A.

13
00:00:52.499 --> 00:00:57.821
The leader appends it as entry 1, term 1, and sends it out with AppendEntries.

14
00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.754
S1 and S2 store it.

15
00:00:59.754 --> 00:01:02.984
The messages to S4 and S5 are lost.

16
00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:08.753
Stored on 3 of 5, a majority, pay-A is committed, and the client hears OK.

17
00:01:08.753 --> 00:01:12.280
The next heartbeat brings S4 and S5 up to date.

18
00:01:12.433 --> 00:01:14.332
Now the network cuts S3 off.

19
00:01:14.332 --> 00:01:19.487
It still thinks it leads term 1, and appends pay-B, but no one can store it.

20
00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:21.733
The others hear no heartbeat.

21
00:01:21.733 --> 00:01:26.507
S1 times out, wins term 2 with three more votes, and commits pay-C.

22
00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:28.028
The network heals.

23
00:01:28.028 --> 00:01:32.602
S3 sends a heartbeat for term 1, and the reply carries term 2.

24
00:01:32.602 --> 00:01:36.512
A higher term means a newer leader, so S3 steps down.

25
00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:43.320
S1's log wins: pay-C replaces pay-B, which was never committed, so its client retries.

26
00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:47.896
One leader per term, and an entry counts once a majority stores it.

27
00:01:47.896 --> 00:01:50.127
That keeps all five logs the same.
